# playpick gave mode=battleground map=conquest spec=druid:balance style=mash
# view=844x390,touch save=carried. direction.md's #7 has never seen mash on any
# battleground: reading scripts/playbot.ts's movement branch (line ~928-959)
# first showed mash has no steer term at all -- it is not among the
# dodge/good/melee/wander/flee/learn branches, so `want` stays null and mash
# never moves, but it does press an ability every tick, round-robin, same as
# wander's press logic without wander's own random heading. So this cell tests
# a shape #7 has not: a body that stands still at its starting position (like
# flee/dodge, which never die) but keeps mashing an untargeted ability into
# whatever is nearby (unlike flee/dodge, which never press at all, and unlike
# good/melee, which walk into the fight and die within 15s on every map tried
# so far). Conquest (The Three Cairns) is "hold ground, clock does the rest" --
# a stationary body is at least standing where a capture fight would happen,
# so mashing from a fixed spot might land hits nobody has measured yet.
open
targets
shot front

tap battleground
tap map:conquest
targets
shot conquest-picked

tap class:druid:balance
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
shot pulled
state
targets

play mash 100
shot mid1
state
bill

wait 5
play mash 100
shot mid2
state
bill

wait 5
play mash 100
shot mid3
state
bill
says
targets
